WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.245
Will left to get Paul Revere, and Vinnie and Mandy stayed to help his mother pick apples.

2
00:00:07.246 --> 00:00:11.485
Several large apple trees grew in the backyard.

3
00:00:11.486 --> 00:00:18.357
Will’s mother gave them each a basket, and they all filled them with apples.

4
00:00:18.358 --> 00:00:22.602
As they worked, the children asked about England.

5
00:00:22.603 --> 00:00:28.557
"A while ago, the British passed the Stamp Act," Will’s mother said.

6
00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:32.817
"We heard something about that," said Vinnie.

7
00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:41.226
"Everything we read—newspapers, magazines, books, even playing cards—must have a stamp.

8
00:00:41.227 --> 00:00:44.945
The stamp shows that a tax has been paid for it.

9
00:00:44.946 --> 00:00:50.907
Americans shouldn’t have to pay taxes to the British," she said with feeling.

10
00:00:50.908 --> 00:00:54.858
"That’s not fair," said Mandy.

11
00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:59.984
"Many people are upset," Will’s mother continued.

12
00:00:59.985 --> 00:01:02.384
"And many of us spoke up.

13
00:01:02.385 --> 00:01:07.033
Some Boston men formed a group called the Sons of Liberty."

14
00:01:07.034 --> 00:01:12.484
"Are Mr. Adams and Mr. Hancock members?" asked Vinnie.

15
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:15.599
Will’s mother did not answer.

16
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.027
She said, "It is a secret group.

17
00:01:19.028 --> 00:01:22.294
No one knows for sure who is a member.

18
00:01:22.295 --> 00:01:26.501
But we know they are fighting for America’s freedom."

19
00:01:26.502 --> 00:01:32.368
"Is that why Mr. Hancock was arrested?" asked Mandy.

20
00:01:32.369 --> 00:01:34.733
"I want to show you something,"

21
00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:38.069
Will’s mother said in a direct way.

22
00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:43.345
She carried her basket into the house and down to the basement.

23
00:01:43.346 --> 00:01:45.986
The children followed.

24
00:01:45.987 --> 00:01:50.088
The basement was filled with barrels of apples.

25
00:01:50.089 --> 00:01:56.514
"Wow! What are you going to do with all these apples?" asked Vinnie.

26
00:01:56.515 --> 00:02:00.443
"We make apple cider," she explained.

27
00:02:00.444 --> 00:02:04.688
"Our Boston apple cider is very popular in Europe.

28
00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:07.522
We ship it everywhere."

29
00:02:07.523 --> 00:02:12.664
She proudly showed them a stack of clothes, neatly folded.

30
00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:16.540
"See these clothes?" said Will’s mother.

31
00:02:16.541 --> 00:02:20.007
"Some women and I belong to our own group.

32
00:02:20.008 --> 00:02:22.937
We are called the Daughters of Liberty.

33
00:02:22.938 --> 00:02:25.805
We make all of our own clothes.

34
00:02:25.806 --> 00:02:29.252
We don’t buy any dresses from Britain.

35
00:02:29.253 --> 00:02:34.530
Boston families don’t want or need anything from Britain."

36
00:02:34.531 --> 00:02:37.660
Just then, Will returned.

37
00:02:37.661 --> 00:02:41.488
"We need to go now," he said simply.

38
00:02:41.489 --> 00:02:46.485
Vinnie and Mandy said good-bye to Will’s mother and his sisters.

39
00:02:46.486 --> 00:02:50.045
They followed Will to the center of town.

40
00:02:50.046 --> 00:02:54.731
Beautiful brick homes with stone steps lined the streets.

41
00:02:54.732 --> 00:02:58.309
Some houses also had offices.

42
00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:04.998
They walked up to one office with a sign that read, "John Adams, Attorney."

43
00:03:04.999 --> 00:03:08.180
A servant opened the door.

44
00:03:08.181 --> 00:03:13.372
"Will Coats to see Mr. Adams," Will told the servant.

45
00:03:13.373 --> 00:03:17.608
They followed the servant into an office.

46
00:03:17.609 --> 00:03:22.715
It was beautifully decorated with polished wooden furniture.

47
00:03:22.716 --> 00:03:25.627
Portraits hung on the walls.

48
00:03:25.628 --> 00:03:30.855
"Is Mr. Adams a famous attorney?" asked Mandy.

49
00:03:30.856 --> 00:03:36.446
Will nodded and added, "He is also a fighter for freedom."

50
00:03:36.447 --> 00:03:43.360
"And the second president of the United States," whispered Vinnie to his sister.

51
00:03:43.361 --> 00:03:48.045
Mandy giggled.

52
00:03:48.046 --> 00:03:53.196
The servant led them to two men talking before a fireplace.

53
00:03:53.197 --> 00:03:56.500
They turned when the children walked in.

54
00:03:56.501 --> 00:04:01.627
"Come in!" A man with a sharp, thin nose walked toward them.

55
00:04:01.628 --> 00:04:11.262
"I’m John Adams," he said, "and this is Paul Revere."

